{
  "tag": "React · ES6+",
  "hex": "logo:react",
  "glyph": "logo:react",
  "slides": [
    {
      "title": [
        "Modern",
        "JavaScript"
      ],
      "hsize": 96,
      "illus": "clipboard",
      "sub": "The **ES6+ features** every React dev uses.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "React is just JavaScript. **Learn these 7 features first.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What You'll Learn"
        },
        {
          "type": "cards",
          "cols": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "color": "blue",
              "icon": "lock",
              "title": "1. let / const",
              "text": "Safer variables"
            },
            {
              "color": "green",
              "icon": "zap",
              "title": "2. Arrow functions",
              "text": "Short callbacks"
            },
            {
              "color": "orange",
              "icon": "box",
              "title": "3. Destructuring",
              "text": "Unpack props and state"
            },
            {
              "color": "purple",
              "icon": "copy",
              "title": "4. Spread / Rest",
              "text": "Copy, merge, collect"
            },
            {
              "color": "red",
              "icon": "list",
              "title": "5. map()",
              "text": "Turn data into JSX"
            },
            {
              "color": "blue",
              "icon": "filter",
              "title": "6. filter()",
              "text": "Keep what matches"
            },
            {
              "color": "green",
              "icon": "refresh",
              "title": "7. Promises",
              "text": "Handle async work"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        "let, const &",
        "Arrow Functions"
      ],
      "hsize": 78,
      "illus": "laptop_code",
      "sub": "Two small changes: **safer, shorter code**.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sections",
          "items": [
            {
              "color": "blue",
              "title": "1. let & const",
              "text": "Use `const` by default. Use `let` only when it changes.",
              "code": [
                "const name = \"Ali\";",
                "let count = 0;",
                "count = count + 1;",
                "// name = \"Sam\"  -> TypeError"
              ]
            },
            {
              "color": "green",
              "title": "2. Arrow functions",
              "text": "Shorter syntax for callbacks and components.",
              "code": [
                "const add = (a, b) => a + b;",
                "",
                "const Hello = ({ name }) => (",
                "  <h1>Hello, {name}</h1>",
                ");"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "takeaway",
          "text": "Skip `var`. Arrow functions keep callbacks **short and clean**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        "Destructuring",
        "Spread & Rest"
      ],
      "hsize": 84,
      "illus": "laptop_dark",
      "sub": "Unpack, copy and merge **without mutating**.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sections",
          "items": [
            {
              "color": "orange",
              "title": "1. Destructuring",
              "text": "Pull values out of objects and arrays.",
              "code": [
                "const { name, age } = user;",
                "const [count, setCount] = useState(0);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "color": "purple",
              "title": "2. Spread",
              "text": "Copy or merge into a new value.",
              "code": [
                "const next = { ...user, age: 30 };",
                "const all = [...items, newItem];"
              ]
            },
            {
              "color": "blue",
              "title": "3. Rest",
              "text": "Collect what is left over.",
              "code": [
                "const { id, ...others } = props;",
                "const [first, ...rest] = [1, 2, 3];"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "takeaway",
          "text": "Spread builds a **new object**. That keeps React state immutable."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        "map() &",
        "filter()"
      ],
      "illus": "laptop_list",
      "sub": "Both return a **new array**.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sections",
          "items": [
            {
              "color": "green",
              "title": "1. map()",
              "text": "Transform every item.",
              "code": [
                "const names = users.map(u => u.name);"
              ],
              "result": "Result: [\"Ali\", \"Sara\", \"Omar\"]"
            },
            {
              "color": "orange",
              "title": "2. filter()",
              "text": "Keep only the items that match.",
              "code": [
                "const on = users.filter(u => u.active);"
              ],
              "result": "Result: only the active users"
            },
            {
              "color": "blue",
              "title": "3. In JSX",
              "text": "Chain both to render a list.",
              "code": [
                "users",
                "  .filter(u => u.active)",
                "  .map(u => <li key={u.id}>{u.name}</li>)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "takeaway",
          "text": "Neither changes the original array. **Always add a key.**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        "Promises &",
        "async / await"
      ],
      "hsize": 84,
      "illus": "laptop_async",
      "sub": "Handle API calls **without freezing the UI**.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "flow",
          "seps": [
            "arrow",
            "or"
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "color": "orange",
              "icon": "clock",
              "title": "Pending",
              "text": "Request in progress"
            },
            {
              "color": "green",
              "icon": "check",
              "title": "Fulfilled",
              "text": "You get the data"
            },
            {
              "color": "red",
              "icon": "x",
              "title": "Rejected",
              "text": "You get an error"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sections",
          "items": [
            {
              "color": "blue",
              "title": "1. .then()",
              "text": "Chain steps one after another.",
              "code": [
                "fetch(\"/api/users\")",
                "  .then(res => res.json())",
                "  .then(setUsers);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "color": "green",
              "title": "2. async/await",
              "text": "Same result, reads top to bottom.",
              "code": [
                "async function load() {",
                "  const res = await fetch(\"/api/users\");",
                "  setUsers(await res.json());",
                "}"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "takeaway",
          "text": "Wrap `await` in **try / catch** for the rejected case."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        "Putting It All",
        "Together"
      ],
      "hsize": 82,
      "illus": "flow",
      "sub": "One component using **every feature**.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sections",
          "items": [
            {
              "color": "purple",
              "title": "1. Render",
              "text": "const, arrow, destructuring, filter, map, spread.",
              "code": [
                "const List = ({ users }) =>",
                "  users",
                "    .filter(u => u.active)",
                "    .map(u => <Card key={u.id} {...u} />);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "color": "blue",
              "title": "2. Load",
              "text": "Promises fetch the data.",
              "code": [
                "useEffect(() => {",
                "  fetch(\"/api/users\")",
                "    .then(res => res.json())",
                "    .then(setUsers);",
                "}, []);"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "takeaway",
          "icon": "target",
          "label": "Your turn:",
          "text": "**Which feature do you use most?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "profile"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}